/ref 1045 "Simplifying Rational Expressions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054920 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186055660 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054920 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050843 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054920 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "2d0c79d2-d7c8-5c21-8622-ee767a7a7c30" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055415 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186053727 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055415 #edb/ref 1069 "q-57766" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055415 #edb/ref 1071 "What is $(10x)/(12(x + 1))$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055415 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c99039b2-017b-5b94-ab7c-1d3602f59629" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055660 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055779 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055660 #edb/ref 1061 2840 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055660 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f4f7f7d8-d9a6-5429-90e3-be9b91605346" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055660 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186055937 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055661 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055662 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055661 #edb/ref 1061 2841 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055661 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1d739d52-799e-5346-b39c-0b0645832542" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055661 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186054690 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055662 #edb/ref 1061 2844 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055662 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "33c7bbb7-80a6-54b5-947c-b818c0f0815b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055662 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186054691 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055778 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055661 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055778 #edb/ref 1061 5177 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055778 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8f0e5b5a-29ee-5e7c-8be7-1d875b8af159" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055778 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186054767 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055779 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055778 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055779 #edb/ref 1061 5178 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055779 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "35ede038-3fa2-5835-8700-2b38ac1cd752" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055779 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186054768 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055937 #edb/ref 1064 "If a rational expression is expressed in factored form, we can sometimes make the expression even simpler by pulling out factors that are common in both the numerator and denominator.\n\nFor example, suppose that we want to simplify the rational expression\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4(2x-3)}{2}\n$$\n\nIf we decompose $4$ into $2\\cdot 2$, we can pull out a factor of $2$ from both the numerator and denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(4(2x - 3))/(2) &=  \\\\\n(2 \\cdot 2 \\cdot (2x - 3))/(2) &=  \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{2} \\cdot (2 \\cdot (2x - 3))/(1)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe fraction\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2}{2}\n$$\n\nis the same as $1$, and anything times $1$ is just itself, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{2}{2} \\cdot (2 \\cdot (2x - 3))/(1) &=  \\\\\n1 \\cdot (2 \\cdot (2x - 3))/(1) &=  \\\\\n&= (2 \\cdot (2x - 3))/(1) \\\\\n&= 2(2x - 3)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** There is a shortcut! We can just \"cancel\" a $2$ from the numerator and denominator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(4(2x - 3))/(2) &=  \\\\\n(2 \\cdot 2 \\cdot (2x - 3))/(2) &=  \\\\\n(2 \\cdot 2 \\cdot (2x - 3))/(2) &=  \\\\\n(2 \\cdot (2x - 3))/(1) &=  \\\\\n&= 2(2x - 3)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055937 #edb/ref 1065 1369 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055937 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "5a1da69d-c5e3-5832-9f42-e75315b6c1a4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055937 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
